step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a simple robust mean of all models in pool_full to see baseline performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse error weights on the full pool to see if it improves over the plain mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a median combination on the full pool to see if a robust non‑linear aggregator improves over mean/weighted.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on the full pool to see if robust trimming improves over weighted inverse error.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test the best single model hypothesis by using ETS alone to see if a single strong model outperforms the robust combinations.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ETS"}

Thought: Test a robust dba combination on the full model pool to see if it outperforms the best single ETS.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a weighted inverse-error combination on the smaller, more stable pool1 to see if restricting models improves performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple mean on the smaller, more stable pool1 to see if reducing model set improves robustness.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the pooled_meta_model weights (w1) on the full model pool to see if a learned meta-weighting improves over the best single ETS.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Evaluate a simple mean on the medium‐sized pool2 to see if adding FT_rf improves robustness over the full pool mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Try a median aggregation on pool2 to see if a robust non‑linear combiner on a more focused set improves over mean and weighted attempts.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on the smaller, stable pool1 to see if trimming improves robustness over mean/weighted on that pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool1","trim_pct":0.2}

